IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg8-s267-parent-and-subsidiary-merger`

-- Tests of section 267 (merger of parent entity and subsidiary corporation or corporations).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the text of section 267 (src:1372-1380) and written here before running; none was copied from the code's output.

§ `Builders`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation`
`t267 class` a b c d MEANS
    `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation` WITH
        `the corporation has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)` IS a
        , `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS b
        , `the number of outstanding shares of the class` IS c
        , `the number of those shares owned by the entity` IS d

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 267(a) Certifications in the certificate of ownership and merger`
`t267 certifications` a b c MEANS
    `s 267(a) Certifications in the certificate of ownership and merger` WITH
        `s 267(a)(b)(i) the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity is formed or organized` IS a
        , `s 267(a)(b)(ii) the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger` IS b
        , `s 267(a)(A) the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party upon surrender of each share not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of those shares` IS c

§ `s 267(d)`

-- Text, (d)(2): "Entity" means a partnership (general, limited, LLP, LLLP), limited liability company, joint-stock association or company, and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or
-- outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest. A corporation is not one; a natural person is not one. Arguments: the kind, whether it has members or evidences of interest.
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a general partnership` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a limited partnership` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a limited liability partnership` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a limited liability limited partnership` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a limited liability company` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a joint-stock association` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a statutory trust` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a business trust or association` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a real estate investment trust` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a common-law trust` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `any other unincorporated business or association` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a statutory trust` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a business trust or association` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a real estate investment trust` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a common-law trust` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `any other unincorporated business or association` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` (`a corporation` `a stock corporation`) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` (`a corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` `a natural person` TRUE)

-- Text, (d)(1): "Constituent party" means an entity or corporation to be merged pursuant to this section. Arguments: the kind, whether it has members or evidences of interest, whether it is to be merged.
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` (`a corporation` `a stock corporation`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` `a limited liability company` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` `a statutory trust` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` (`a corporation` `a stock corporation`) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` `a statutory trust` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` `a natural person` FALSE TRUE)

-- Text, (d)(3): "Governing documents" means a partnership agreement, limited liability company agreement, articles of association or any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized.
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `a partnership agreement under s 267(d)(3)`
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `a limited liability company agreement under s 267(d)(3)`
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `articles of association under s 267(d)(3)`
#ASSERT `s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `an instrument that does not contain the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)`)

§ `s 267(a)(1)`

-- Text: a class counts if it has outstanding shares that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger, and its corporation does not have the section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) provision.
-- Arguments to the class builder: has the 251(g)(7) provision, has shares that would be entitled to vote, outstanding shares, shares owned by the entity.
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 90)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` (`t267 class` TRUE TRUE 100 90))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` (`t267 class` FALSE FALSE 100 90))
-- Text: "at least 90%": reaching 90 percent is enough; 89 of 100 is not.
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 90) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 89) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 91) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 0) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 10 9) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 1000 899) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- counts that cannot be a holding are not covered: more owned than outstanding; no outstanding shares
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 101) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Text: "of each class": every counting class must reach 90 percent
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 50 45)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 50 44)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 85), (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 50 50)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a class whose corporation has the 251(g)(7) provision, or that has no shares that would be entitled to vote, is left out of the test
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` TRUE TRUE 50 1)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` FALSE FALSE 50 1)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- nothing to measure: no class counts, or no classes at all: not covered
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` TRUE TRUE 50 50)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE FALSE 50 50)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- a counting class with counts that cannot be a holding: not covered; the same counts in a class left out do not matter
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 10 11)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST (`t267 class` FALSE TRUE 100 95), (`t267 class` TRUE TRUE 10 11)) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 267(a)(2) and the power`

-- Text: "1 or more of such corporations is a corporation of this State".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a)(2) 1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` 0)
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(2) 1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` 1
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(2) 1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` 3
-- Text: where (1) and (2) hold, "unless the laws of the jurisdiction ... prohibit such merger, the entity ... may" merge. Arguments: (1) result, (2), prohibition.
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 267(a) the certificate of ownership and merger`

-- Text: the merger is authorized under the entity's governing documents and law, and a certificate of ownership and merger is acknowledged and filed (section 103), certifying (i) the authorization (executed under the
-- entity's documents and law) and (ii) the type of entity of each constituent entity; and, if the entity does not own all the stock, (A) states the terms and conditions.
-- Arguments: authorized, filed under section 103, executed as required, entity owns all the stock, then the three certifications ((b)(i), (b)(ii), (A)).
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`t267 certifications` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`t267 certifications` FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`t267 certifications` TRUE FALSE FALSE))

-- Text: the entity "may either merge the corporation or corporations into itself ... or merge itself ... into 1 of the other corporations": in the first the entity survives, in the second a corporation does.
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the entity is the surviving constituent party` `the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the entity is the surviving constituent party` `the entity merges itself, or itself and 1 or more of the corporations, into 1 of the other corporations`)

-- Text, the proviso (B): where the entity does not own all the stock, the terms "may not result in a holder of stock in a corporation becoming a general partner in a surviving entity that is a partnership
-- (other than a limited liability partnership or a limited liability limited partnership)". Arguments: the entity owns all the stock, the terms make a holder a general partner, the kind of the surviving entity.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE TRUE `a general partnership`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE TRUE `a limited partnership`)
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE TRUE `a limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE TRUE `a limited liability limited partnership`
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE TRUE `a limited liability company`
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` FALSE FALSE `a general partnership`
-- when the entity owns all the stock the proviso is not engaged
#ASSERT `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` TRUE TRUE `a general partnership`

-- Text: terms dependent on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger, provided the manner is clearly and expressly set forth in it.
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` FALSE FALSE

-- Text: "If the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State, (1) § 252(d) shall also apply ...; (2) the terms and conditions ... shall obligate the surviving constituent party".
#ASSERT `s 267(a) section 252(d) also applies to the merger` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) section 252(d) also applies to the merger` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the word corporation in section 252(d) is deemed to include the entity` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the word corporation in section 252(d) is deemed to include the entity` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the word corporation in section 252(d) is deemed to include the entity` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party as section 252(d) requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(a) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party as section 252(d) requires` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party as section 252(d) requires` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 267(b) and (c)`

-- Text, (b): sections 259, 261 and 328 apply insofar as applicable; sections 260 and 251(e) apply to a merger in which the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State.
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 259 as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 261 as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 328 as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 259 as applied by s 267(b)` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 260 as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 260 as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)` FALSE TRUE)
-- Text, (b): "references to “agreement of merger” in § 251(e) shall mean the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger, and references to “corporation” in §§ 259-261 ... and § 328 ... shall be deemed to include the entity, as applicable".
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the way the reference is read` `the words agreement of merger in s 251(e)` EQUALS `the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger`
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the way the reference is read` `the word corporation in ss 259 to 261` EQUALS `a corporation or, as applicable, the entity`
#ASSERT `s 267(b) the way the reference is read` `the word corporation in s 328` EQUALS `a corporation or, as applicable, the entity`
-- Text, (b) last sentence and (c): section 262 does not apply, except that where all the stock was not owned by the entity immediately before the merger the stockholders have appraisal rights as section 262 sets out.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(b) section 262 applies to the merger` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 267(b) section 262 applies to the merger` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 267(c) the stockholders of the Delaware corporation have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 267(c) the stockholders of the Delaware corporation have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262` FALSE

§ `The meaning of "facts" (s 267(a))`

-- Text (src:1373): the term "facts" "includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the entity".
-- An event, a determination by any person or body and an action by any person or body are facts; for anything else the text does not say (NOTHING; fork F26).
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the occurrence of an event under s 267(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `a determination by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `an action by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 267(a)` EQUALS NOTHING
